{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1779282707025,"sessionID":"ses_1ba7d2979ffeuVyupLTjsOevTe","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"glob","callID":"tool_glob_JuHYuTnbZtzeBWxfoUsy","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"cores/**/rtl/*div*"},"output":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gemini-3_5-flash-rep2/cores/v1/rtl/div_unit.sv\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gemini-3_5-flash-rep2/cores/ibex/rtl/ibex_multdiv_slow.sv\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gemini-3_5-flash-rep2/cores/ibex/rtl/ibex_multdiv_fast.sv","metadata":{"count":3,"truncated":false},"title":"","time":{"start":1779282707006,"end":1779282707023}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"**Refining ALU Division Logic**\n\nI'm focusing on optimizing the combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU operations within `rtl/alu.sv`. My current direction is to integrate a compact iterative RV32M divide/remainder unit and implement an EX-stage interlock exclusively for these specific opcodes, as noted in `cores/v1/experiments/log.jsonl`.\n\n**Rethinking ALU Division**\n\nI've confirmed that the division and remainder operations in `cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv` are currently fully combinational. This deep combinational logic is significantly impacting Fmax, so I'm exploring the idea of isolating these operations to reduce the critical path.\n\n","format":"google-gemini-v1","index":0},{"type":"reasoning.encrypted","data":"","id":"tool_glob_JuHYuTnbZtzeBWxfoUsy","format":"google-gemini-v1","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_e45838237001GI3j90fQKEz6Wg","sessionID":"ses_1ba7d2979ffeuVyupLTjsOevTe","messageID":"msg_e45837276001STX3fj9WAQPLJ7"}}
