ch rule. A quick dynamic profile of the timed\\nCoreMark region shows that the baseline BTFNT rule is especially wrong for\\ntwo simple branch classes: backward BEQ branches, which are mostly not taken\\nin this binary, and forward BNE branches, which are usually taken. Those two\\nclasses account for a large fraction of residual static predictor mistakes,\\nand they can be recognized from the funct3 bits already examined in IF for\\nbranch legality. This targets iterations/cycle without adding a predictor\\nRAM, update feedback path, BTB, RAS, or extra target adder.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current best frontend already has the two predictor features that have\\nactually paid off: backward conditional branches predict taken, and direct\\nJAL targets are predicted in IF. The learned predictor attempts point in the\\nother direction: both the 64-entry agree table and the 16-entry forward-only\\noverride table reduced CoreMark cycles, but their table read/update routing\\ncost more Fmax than the saved mispredicts recovered. Return prediction was\\neven less attractive after the post-DIV timing win, with only small cycle\\nsavings and a large clock regression.\\n\\nThe remaining p... (line truncated to 2000 chars)","truncated":true,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/v1/experiments/log.jsonl","time":{"start":1779282727063,"end":1779282727067}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.encrypted","data":"AY89a1+NBk7c8dAcBya0Mz8wemIF24kovhxlY3Cqp9sAqtnl0GWJbcLBBBfNRd6X7D3FP7akpSO4BDGlLdxk3NKME20TKrowPPgCUMoxTaWSVDEc7QWx9w8QHIsZyh2PlnVqBbJR5fQKqSZKI/Tbo7vZH07U/deJ592Sj/ABeCRUFZlHFOK75Fj0jf20XOr5ZmVplCJOcw/suq22ynR7Ew1U/7ThuhCK2hCCLLu1eBHG2iy894HV+LKkrp/61Z9KR4gp5G6f","id":"tool_read_vY3uSt8nrIZ1UXuzn6cs","format":"google-gemini-v1","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_e4583d095001VO6JBAKzFVlwTz","sessionID":"ses_1ba7d2979ffeuVyupLTjsOevTe","messageID":"msg_e4583c2f9001B62PN2bkxk52D6"}}
