-risk micro-optimization than the prior failed\\nDIV/REM interlock attempt because it leaves divider behavior, pipeline stalls,\\nand RVFI ordering untouched.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the three unconditional multiplier expressions in rtl/alu.sv with a\\nsingle shared 33-bit-by-33-bit product. For MUL, zero-extend both operands and\\nuse the low 32 bits; for MULH, sign-extend both operands; for MULHSU,\\nsign-extend rs1 and zero-extend rs2; for MULHU, zero-extend both operands.\\nSelect product[63:32] for the high-half operations and product[31:0] for MUL.\\nKeep the RISC...","metadata":{"matches":1,"truncated":false},"title":"\"id\": \"hyp-20260427-004-r2s0\"","time":{"start":1779282760483,"end":1779282760489}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"**Investigating Micro Opt Categorization**\n\nI'm currently reviewing recent logs, specifically looking at entries categorized as \"micro_opt\" to understand why they didn't match existing patterns. My next step is to either utilize the `read` tool or conduct a manual search within `cores/v1/experiments` to pinpoint relevant lines and their outcomes.\n\n","format":"google-gemini-v1","index":0},{"type":"reasoning.encrypted","data":"","id":"tool_grep_hYdwl8vawcFkQqLlNVn0","format":"google-gemini-v1","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_e45845320001pKiXghEe9JVdXm","sessionID":"ses_1ba7d2979ffeuVyupLTjsOevTe","messageID":"msg_e4584308f001IagmmypvbpY2R8"}}
