{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1779280233043,"sessionID":"ses_1baa43cbeffe3Tj2jTU7G2nLIP","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"tool_write_6o8wU0JOuOFCnl6orV6r","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"id: hyp-20260520-002-r1s1\ntitle: \"One-Deep Store Retirement Slot With Direct Fast Path\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The baseline 5-stage core treats every dmem-not-ready cycle on a store as a\n  full pipeline freeze, even though a store's data and byte mask are already\n  known in MEM and no register result is needed by younger ALU/control\n  instructions. Under the tournament's random dmem stalls (~22%), this turns\n  store bus backpressure into lost execute bandwidth. A timing-local,\n  one-deep pending-store slot will decouple execute from these memory stalls,\n  significantly improving iterations per cycle (IPC) on store-heavy paths\n  without adding Fmax pressure.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a one-deep pending-store retirement slot that is used only on a legal,\n  aligned normal-RAM store when io_dmemReady is low. When io_dmemReady is high\n  and the slot is empty, stores drive the existing dmem outputs directly and\n  retire exactly as they do today. When io_dmemReady is low, the MEM stage\n  captures the store address, replicated write data, byte mask, and RVFI memory\n  metadata into the slot, retires that store once through MEM/WB, and lets\n  younger non-memory instructions continue while the slot drains. Younger\n  loads, younger stores, and all MMIO/marker/UART stores stall until the\n  pending store drains, preserving in-order memory visibility and exact\n  timing-marker behavior.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/store_slot.sv\n    description: \"Add a one-entry pending-store slot with valid, enqueue, drain-valid, and drain-ready controls.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Split store completion into a direct fast path and a low-ready enqueue path.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Replace the generic dmem-stall predicate with MEM-stage wait inputs to allow younger non-memory instructions to proceed during store drains.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Instantiate the pending-store slot and arbitrate the top-level dmem port between MEM stage and the slot.\"\n","filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gemini-3_5-flash-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260520-002-r1s1.yaml"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gemini-3_5-flash-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260520-002-r1s1.yaml","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260520-002-r1s1.yaml","time":{"start":1779280233040,"end":1779280233042}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"**Committing changes to YAML**\n\nI've successfully created the hypothesis YAML file in the specified directory. The working tree is now clean, and I'm ready for the next step in the process.\n\n","format":"google-gemini-v1","index":0},{"type":"reasoning.encrypted","data":"","id":"tool_write_6o8wU0JOuOFCnl6orV6r","format":"google-gemini-v1","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_e455dc24d001mPmzUd7XAkgaUP","sessionID":"ses_1baa43cbeffe3Tj2jTU7G2nLIP","messageID":"msg_e455dadee0019fHM0kf2TTzMaf"}}
