{"type":"text","timestamp":1779280238079,"sessionID":"ses_1baa43cbeffe3Tj2jTU7G2nLIP","part":{"id":"prt_e455dd244001QNgPmIN1WuHCpR","messageID":"msg_e455dc3fa001tl2MA0xImYw5L7","sessionID":"ses_1baa43cbeffe3Tj2jTU7G2nLIP","type":"text","text":"I have analyzed the historical outcomes and identified the most promising structural optimization for the baseline `cores/bench/` core: a **One-Deep Store Retirement Slot With Direct Fast Path**. \n\nThis optimization targets store-heavy dmem stalls under the tournament's random ~22% dmem backpressure. Instead of stalling the whole pipeline immediately on every dmem-not-ready cycle of a store, the MEM stage enqueues the store into a timing-local one-entry buffer slot, retires it through MEM/WB, and allows younger non-memory instructions to proceed. The slot then drains asynchronously once the dmem port unblocks.\n\nThe hypothesis has been written to the required path:\n`cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260520-002-r1s1.yaml`","time":{"start":1779280237124,"end":1779280238077}}}
