d\\nretire exactly as they do today. When io_dmemReady is low, the MEM stage\\ncaptures the store address, replicated write data, byte mask, and RVFI memory\\nmetadata into the slot, retires that store once through MEM/WB, and lets\\nyounger non-memory instructions continue while the slot drains. Younger\\nloads, younger stores, and all MMIO/marker/UART stores stall until the\\npending store drains, preserving in-order memory visibility and exact\\ntiming-marker behavior.\\n\", \"expected_im...","metadata":{"matches":1,"truncated":false},"title":"hyp-20260520-002-r1s1","time":{"start":1779282684165,"end":1779282684176}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"**Analyzing Log Data**\n\nI'm sifting through `cores/v1/experiments/log.jsonl`, specifically examining `hyp-20260428-017-r8s1`. This entry, categorized as \"structural,\" is showing a promising +5.89% improvement, and I'm keen to understand its implications further.\n\n","format":"google-gemini-v1","index":0},{"type":"reasoning.encrypted","data":"","id":"tool_grep_QQJ6vWBFqOCiMPzNyWVu","format":"google-gemini-v1","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_e45832902001lbL52UNPIevf4p","sessionID":"ses_1ba7d2a2bffepcCr3DVoK1N8UH","messageID":"msg_e458314bf00117S4XmXavLrwjr"}}
