{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1779282696310,"sessionID":"ses_1ba7d2a2bffepcCr3DVoK1N8UH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"tool_bash_v0H3sU4yTXoOBqCoHMFE","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"python temp_parse_bench.py","description":"Runs Python script to parse and print full details of hyp-20260520-002-r1s1 from cores/bench log.jsonl"},"output":"{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20260520-002-r1s1\",\n  \"title\": \"One-Deep Store Retirement Slot With Direct Fast Path\",\n  \"category\": \"structural\",\n  \"motivation\": \"The baseline 5-stage core treats every dmem-not-ready cycle on a store as a\\nfull pipeline freeze, even though a store's data and byte mask are already\\nknown in MEM and no register result is needed by younger ALU/control\\ninstructions. Under the tournament's random dmem stalls (~22%), this turns\\nstore bus backpressure into lost execute bandwidth. A timing-local,\\none-deep pending-store slot will decouple execute from these memory stalls,\\nsignificantly improving iterations per cycle (IPC) on store-heavy paths\\nwithout adding Fmax pressure.\\n\",\n  \"hypothesis\": {\n    \"motivation\": \"The baseline 5-stage core treats every dmem-not-ready cycle on a store as a\\nfull pipeline freeze, even though a store's data and byte mask are already\\nknown in MEM and no register result is needed by younger ALU/control\\ninstructions. Under the tournament's random dmem stalls (~22%), this turns\\nstore bus backpressure into lost execute bandwidth. A timing-local,\\none-deep pending-store slot will decouple execute from these memory stalls,\\nsignificantly improving iterations per cycle (IPC) on store-heavy paths\\nwithout adding Fmax pressure.\\n\",\n    \"hypothesis\": \"Add a one-deep pending-store retirement slot that is used only on a legal,\\naligned normal-RAM store when io_dmemReady is low. When io_dmemReady is high\\nand the slot is empty, stores drive the existing dmem outputs directly and\\nretire exactly as they do today. When io_dmemReady is low, the MEM stage\\ncaptures the store address, replicated write data, byte mask, and RVFI memory\\nmetadata into the slot, retires that store once through MEM/WB, and lets\\nyounger non-memory instructions continue while the slot drains. Younger\\nloads, younger stores, and all MMIO/marker/UART stores stall until the\\npending store drains, preserving in-order memory visibility and exact\\ntiming-marker behavior.\\n\",\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"fitness_delta_pct\": 5,\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    \"changes\": [\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/store_slot.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Add a one-entry pending-store slot with valid, enqueue, drain-valid, and drain-ready controls.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Split store completion into a direct fast path and a low-ready enqueue path.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Replace the generic dmem-stall predicate with MEM-stage wait inputs to allow younger non-memory instructions to proceed during store drains.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Instantiate the pending-store slot and arbitrate the top-level dmem port between MEM stage and the slot.\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"expected_impact\": {\n    \"fitness_delta_pct\": 5,\n    \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  \"changes\": [\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/store_slot.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Add a one-entry pending-store slot with valid, enqueue, drain-valid, and drain-ready controls.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Split store completion into a direct fast path and a low-ready enqueue path.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Replace the generic dmem-stall predicate with MEM-stage wait inputs to allow younger non-memory instructions to proceed during store drains.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Instantiate the pending-store slot and arbitrate the top-level dmem port between MEM stage and the slot.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"outcome\": \"regression\",\n  \"fitness\": 282.82,\n  \"delta_pct\": 0.0,\n  \"vs_baseline\": 0.0,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 127.03,\n  \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06,\n  \"cycles\": 4491485,\n  \"iterations\": 10,\n  \"lut4\": 9563,\n  \"ff\": 1866,\n  \"seeds\": [\n    128.72,\n    127.03,\n    123.02\n  ],\n  \"formal_passed\": true,\n  \"cosim_passed\": true,\n  \"error\": null,\n  \"implementation_notes\": \"\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-20T12:35:19.227416Z\",\n  \"slot\": 1,\n  \"round_id\": 1,\n  \"scribe_skipped\": \"CalledProcessError: Command '['opencode', 'run', 'You are a scribe distilling one-line research lessons.\\\\n\\\\nA CPU microarchitecture experiment just finished on cores/bench/. Your job\\\\nis to append AT MOST ONE bullet to cores/bench/LESSONS.md summarizing what\\\\nwas learned, OR write nothing at all if no useful lesson can be distilled.\\\\n\\\\n## This iteration\\\\n\\\\n- id:        hyp-20260520-002-r1s1\\\\n- title:     One-Deep Store Retirement Slot With Direct Fast Path\\\\n- category:  structural\\\\n- outcome:   regression\\\\n- fitness:   282.82\\\\n- delta_pct: +0.00%\\\\n- error:     none\\\\n\\\\nMotivation:\\\\nThe baseline 5-stage core treats every dmem-not-ready cycle on a store as a\\\\nfull pipeline freeze, even though a store\\\\'s data and byte mask are already\\\\nknown in MEM and no register result is needed by younger ALU/control\\\\ninstructions. Under the tournament\\\\'s random dmem stalls (~22%), this turns\\\\nstore bus backpressure into lost execute bandwidth. A timing-local,\\\\none-deep pending-store slot will decouple execute from these memory stalls,\\\\nsignificantly improving iterations per cycle (IPC) on store-heavy paths\\\\nwithout adding Fmax pressure.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nHypothesis:\\\\nAdd a one-deep p