{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1779282704350,"sessionID":"ses_1ba7d2a2bffepcCr3DVoK1N8UH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"tool_bash_7AS1tix4M2N8vGhYlzVy","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"python temp_parse_bench_3.py","description":"Runs Python script to parse and print full details of hyp-20260520-003-r1s2 from cores/bench log.jsonl"},"output":"{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20260520-003-r1s2\",\n  \"title\": \"Two-bank registered lookahead instruction replay predictor with static branch/JAL predecode\",\n  \"category\": \"predictor\",\n  \"motivation\": \"The baseline RV32IM core always fetches sequentially and resolves all control flow in EX, incurring a 2-cycle flush penalty on every taken branch and jump. Additionally, the apples-to-apples evaluation environment drives ~22% random instruction-memory stalls, injecting significant bubble counts into the pipeline. Conventional branch predictors or target buffers often regress FPGA Fmax by putting instruction decode, target adders, tag comparisons, or return-address stacks directly on the timing-sensitive fetch next-PC path.\\n\",\n  \"hypothesis\": {\n    \"motivation\": \"The baseline RV32IM core always fetches sequentially and resolves all control flow in EX, incurring a 2-cycle flush penalty on every taken branch and jump. Additionally, the apples-to-apples evaluation environment drives ~22% random instruction-memory stalls, injecting significant bubble counts into the pipeline. Conventional branch predictors or target buffers often regress FPGA Fmax by putting instruction decode, target adders, tag comparisons, or return-address stacks directly on the timing-sensitive fetch next-PC path.\\n\",\n    \"hypothesis\": \"We propose a timing-clean, high-performance two-bank registered lookahead instruction replay predictor combined with stateless static branch/JAL predecode in the IF stage:\\n1. Replay Table: A 256-entry (128 per bank), two-bank direct-mapped replay table indexed by pc[8:2] and tagged by pc[31:9]. It caches successfully fetched instruction words and looks up the next-PC replay candidate one cycle ahead, completely removing table reads and tag comparisons from the same-cycle IF decision path.\\n2. iStall Hiding: When imem_ready drops, IF supplies the registered lookahead instruction and asserts fetch-ready, converting random iStall bubbles into zero-wait fetch cycles.\\n3. Static Predecode: Within IF, combinationally predecode JAL and backward conditional branches (negative displacement) from the fetched/replayed instruction, update the fetch next_pc early, and propagate the prediction.\\n4. EX Validation: EX verifies the prediction and asserts redirect only on a mismatch (mispredict), turning correct predictions into 0-cycle control transfers.\\n\",\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"fitness_delta_pct\": 12,\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    \"changes\": [\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Extend if_id_t and id_ex_t with predicted_taken and predicted_target fields.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Implement the static branch/JAL predecode, the 2-bank 128-set registered lookahead instruction replay predictor (tag/valid/instr/mru arrays), and lookahead candidate tracking.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Latch the predicted next-PC metadata fields into the ID/EX register.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Replace unconditional branch/jump redirects with mispredict-only redirection.\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"expected_impact\": {\n    \"fitness_delta_pct\": 12,\n    \"confidence\": \"high\"\n  },\n  \"changes\": [\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Extend if_id_t and id_ex_t with predicted_taken and predicted_target fields.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Implement the static branch/JAL predecode, the 2-bank 128-set registered lookahead instruction replay predictor (tag/valid/instr/mru arrays), and lookahead candidate tracking.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Latch the predicted next-PC metadata fields into the ID/EX register.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Replace unconditional branch/jump redirects with mispredict-only redirection.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"outcome\": \"improvement\",\n  \"fitness\": 359.04,\n  \"delta_pct\": 26.95,\n  \"vs_baseline\": 26.95,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 124.66,\n  \"ipc_coremark\": 3e-06,\n  \"cycles\": 3472016,\n  \"iterations\": 10,\n  \"lut4\": 13773,\n  \"ff\": 3692,\n  \"seeds\": [\n    131.98,\n    124.66,\n    123.64\n  ],\n  \"formal_passed\": true,\n  \"cosim_passed\": true,\n  \"error\": null,\n  \"implementation_notes\": \"\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-20T13:07:09.428474Z\",\n  \"slot\": 2,\n  \"round_id\": 1,\n  \"scribe_skipped\": \"PermissionError: scribe touched off-limits paths and was rolled back: ['find_results.py', 'list_v1_cycles.py', 'read_agent_actions.py', 'read_v1_hyp.py', 'search_bench_results.py']\"\n}\n","metadata":{"output":"{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20260520-003-r1s2\",\n  \"title\": \"Two-bank registered lookahead instruction replay predictor with static branch/JAL predecode\",\n  \"category\": \"predictor\",\n  \"motivation\": \"The baseline RV32IM core always fetches sequentially and resolves all control flow in EX, incurring a 2-cycle flush penalty on every taken branch and jump. Additionally, the apples-to-apples evaluation environment drives ~22% random instruction-memory stalls, injecting significant bubble counts into the pipeline. Conventional branch predictors or target buffers often regress FPGA Fmax by putting instruction decode, target adders, tag comparisons, or return-address stacks directly on the timing-sensitive fetch next-PC path.\\n\",\n  \"hypothesis\": {\n    \"motivation\": \"The baseline RV32IM core always fetches sequentially and resolves all control flow in EX, incurring a 2-cycle flush penalty on every taken branch and jump. Additionally, the apples-to-apples evaluation environment drives ~22% random instruction-memory stalls, injecting significant bubble counts into the pipeline. Conventional branch predictors or target buffers often regress FPGA Fmax by putting instruction decode, target adders, tag comparisons, or return-address stacks directly on the timing-sensitive fetch next-PC path.\\n\",\n    \"hypothesis\": \"We propose a timing-clean, high-performance two-bank registered lookahead instruction replay predictor combined with stateless static branch/JAL predecode in the IF stage:\\n1. Replay Table: A 256-entry (128 per bank), two-bank direct-mapped replay table indexed by pc[8:2] and tagged by pc[31:9]. It caches successfully fetched instruction words and looks up the next-PC replay candidate one cycle ahead, completely removing table reads and tag comparisons from the same-cycle IF decision path.\\n2. iStall Hiding: When imem_ready drops, IF supplies the registered lookahead instruction and asserts fetch-ready, converting random iStall bubbles into zero-wait fetch cycles.\\n3. Static Predecode: Within IF, combinationally predecode JAL and backward conditional branches (negative displacement) from the fetched/replayed instruction, update the fetch next_pc early, and propagate the prediction.\\n4. EX Validation: EX verifies the prediction and asserts redirect only on a mismatch (mispredict), turning correct predictions into 0-cycle control transfers.\\n\",\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"fitness_delta_pct\": 12,\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    \"changes\": [\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Extend if_id_t and id_ex_t with predicted_taken and predicted_target fields.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Implement the static branch/JAL predecode, the 2-bank 128-set registered lookahead instruction replay predictor (tag/valid/instr/mru arrays), and lookahead candidate tracking.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Latch the predicted next-PC metadata fields into the ID/EX register.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Replace unconditional branch/jump redirects with mispredict-only redirection.\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"expected_impact\": {\n    \"fitness_delta_pct\": 12,\n    \"confidence\": \"high\"\n  },\n  \"changes\": [\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Extend if_id_t and id_ex_t with predicted_taken and predicted_target fields.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Implement the static branch/JAL predecode, the 2-bank 128-set registered lookahead instruction replay predictor (tag/valid/instr/mru arrays), and lookahead candidate tracking.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Latch the predicted next-PC metadata fields into the ID/EX register.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Replace unconditional branch/jump redirects with mispredict-only redirection.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"outcome\": \"improvement\",\n  \"fitness\": 359.04,\n  \"delta_pct\": 26.95,\n  \"vs_baseline\": 26.95,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 124.66,\n  \"ipc_coremark\": 3e-06,\n  \"cycles\": 3472016,\n  \"iterations\": 10,\n  \"lut4\": 13773,\n  \"ff\": 3692,\n  \"seeds\": [\n    131.98,\n    124.66,\n    123.64\n  ],\n  \"formal_passed\": true,\n  \"cosim_passed\": true,\n  \"error\": null,\n  \"implementation_notes\": \"\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-20T13:07:09.428474Z\",\n  \"slot\": 2,\n  \"round_id\": 1,\n  \"scribe_skipped\": \"PermissionError: scribe touched off-limits paths and was rolled back: ['find_results.py', 'list_v1_cycles.py', 'read_agent_actions.py', 'read_v1_hyp.py', 'search_bench_results.py']\"\n}\n","exit":0,"description":"Runs Python script to parse and print full details of hyp-20260520-003-r1s2 from cores/bench log.jsonl","truncated":false},"title":"Runs Python script to parse and print full details of hyp-20260520-003-r1s2 from cores/bench log.jsonl","time":{"start":1779282704348,"end":1779282704350}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.encrypted","data":"AY89a19p4ZTdWTdpQZc65gizMoaPke8JqU7djvXD2OwqRCGm6Z3hz0kx19znITUqCKMQ2om1Et0/qO0ardKJzrrtlDsgT7I9iIgj9cL1XJVNbhlLl1HdiOjIMM9TmA+sfylO5eiH/IT30JXZaRa3xrsmXULsUP9JH5maVYDuU05jou5poFP9apeMS7ef3pik5pWOdtYojcxDOB5M1zwj","id":"tool_bash_7AS1tix4M2N8vGhYlzVy","format":"google-gemini-v1","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_e458377c7001L1Pp1w2hNgAeHW","sessionID":"ses_1ba7d2a2bffepcCr3DVoK1N8UH","messageID":"msg_e45836ad3001bimHp15AVgqwHR"}}
