te target prediction into the I-cache (hyp-20260514-003-r9s2)\\nproduced exactly 0 % delta because the predictor valid bit was cleared on every\\ncache refill, so predictions were never visible when the branch PC was fetched again.\\nBy storing a partial tag with each prediction entry and qualifying the hit with\\ntag equality, the predictor state survives across repeated fetches and evictions\\nwithout needing explicit invalidation logic.  This reuses the existing fast I-cache\\nread path (registered state, no external imem_data combinational delay) and adds\\nonly ~250 FFs and a small next-pc mux, well within the remaining LUT4 headroom.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Extend the existing 8-entry I-cache in if_stage.sv with a tiny target predictor:\\n- Add `pred_valid[0:7]`, `pred_tag[0:7]...\n\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gemini-3_5-flash-rep2/bench/kimi-k2_6/rep2/log.jsonl:\n  Line 4: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260513-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"IF-stage static predictor: backward branches and JAL always taken\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline core resolves all control flow in EX, incurring a 2-cycle flush\\npenalty for every taken branch and jump. CoreMark is loop-heavy; loop\\nback-edges are almost always backward branches, and function calls use JAL.\\nPredicting these in IF eliminates the flush penalty for the common case,\\nimproving IPC with minimal additional logic and low Fmax risk.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline core resolves all control flow in EX, incurring a 2-cycle flush\\npenalty for every taken branch and jump. CoreMark is loop-heavy; loop\\nback-edges are almost always backward branches, and function calls use JAL.\\nPredicting these in IF eliminates the flush penalty for the common case,\\nimproving IPC with minimal additional logic and low Fmax risk.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add combinational prediction logic to if_stage.sv that detects JAL (always\\ntaken) and backward B-type branches (negative offset, i.e. imm[31]=1) in the\\nfetched instruction, computes the target address from the immediate, and\\nsteers next_pc to the target when the target is 4-byte aligned. Extend the\\nIF/ID and ID/EX bundles (core_pkg.sv) with predict_taken and predict_target\\nfields. Modify ex_stage.sv to treat a mismatch between predicted and actual\\noutcome as the redirect condition (mispredict), suppressing the flush on\\ncorrect predictions. This turns the common-case loop back-edge and function\\ncall from a 2-cycle bubble into zero penalty.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add predict_taken and predict_target fields to if_id_t and id_ex_t pipeline bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add combinational decode of JAL and backward B-type in fetched instruction, compute target address from immediate, and mux next_pc to the predicted target ...\n  Line 7: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260513-003-r2s2\", \"title\": \"(slot 2 hypothesis-gen failed)\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"hypothesis_gen_failed: Hypothesis agent modified off-limits paths and was rolled back: ['cores/bench/rtl/core.sv']\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 2, \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current static predictor correctly handles JAL and backward branches,\\nbut all JALR returns are unpredicted (fall-through), causing a 2-cycle\\npipeline flush on every function return. CoreMark contains many function\\ncalls and returns; eliminating these mispredictions should improve IPC\\nwith minimal area/Fmax cost.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add an 8-entry Return Address Stack (RAS). In IF, detect JALR with rs1=x1\\nand imm=0 as a return; predict taken to RAS top if the stack is non-empty.\\nIn ID, pop the RAS when a predicted return is captured into the ID/EX\\nregister (gated by !flush so wrong-path returns never corrupt the stack).\\nIn ID, detect JAL/JALR writing x1 as a call and push PC+4 to the RAS\\n(also gated by !flush, and safe because wrong-path instructions are\\nflushed before they reach ID). The RAS is purely a performance\\noptimization; mispredictions are still corrected by the existing EX-stage\\nredirect logic.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ras.sv\", \"description\": \"New 8-entry Return Address Stack module with push/pop/top/empty.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add RAS ports; detect return-pattern JALR (rs1=x1, imm=0); predict taken to RAS top when stack is non-empty; otherwise fall through.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add RAS push/pop ports; detect call (JAL/JALR writing x1) and push PC+4 on capture into ID/EX; detect return and pop RAS on capture when the return was predicted taken; gate both on !flush.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Instantiate RAS and wire push/pop/addr/top/empty between IF, ID and ...\n  Line 10: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260513-003-r3s2\", \"title\": \"4-entry Return Address Stack for JALR returns\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The current static predictor correctly predicts JAL and backward branches,\\nbut every function return (JALR reading x1, writing x0) is predicted\\nnot-taken, incurring a 2-cycle pipeline flush. CoreMark contains frequent\\nfunction calls and returns. A small Return Address Stack predicts return\\naddresses with very high accuracy for minimal area cost, directly\\nimproving IPC without touching the critical EX or MEM paths.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current static predictor correctly predicts JAL and backward branches,\\nbut every function return (JALR reading x1, writing x0) is predicted\\nnot-taken, incurring a 2-cycle pipeline flush. CoreMark contains frequent\\nfunction calls and returns. A small Return Address Stack predicts return\\naddresses with very high accuracy for minimal area cost, directly\\nimproving IPC without touching the critical EX or MEM paths.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a 4-entry Return Address Stack (RAS). In the IF stage, detect\\nreturn-pattern JALR instructions (opcode=JALR, rd=x0, rs1=x1); when the\\nRAS is non-empty, predict taken and steer next_pc to the RAS top entry.\\nIn the ID stage, detect calls (JAL or JALR writing x1) and push PC+4\\nonto the RAS; detect returns and pop the RAS. RAS updates are gated by\\n!flush so wrong-path instructions never corrupt the stack. EX-stage\\nredirect logic continues to verify predictions and correct mispredicts.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ras.sv\", \"description\": \"New 4-entry Return Address Stack module with push/pop/top/empty ports.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Detect return-pattern JALR; when RAS is non-empty assert predict_taken and use ras_top as predict_target.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Detect calls (JAL/JALR writing x1) to push PC+4; detect returns to pop RAS; gate...\n  Line 13: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260514-003-r4s2\", \"title\": \"16-entry bimodal predictor for forward branches\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The existing predictor covers backward branches (always taken), JAL (always\\ntaken), and returns (4-entry RAS). Forward conditional branches are always\\npredicted not-taken. CoreMark contains forward branches in linked-list search\\nand state-machine control flow that are taken frequently, each incurring a\\n2-cycle mispredict penalty. A tiny learned direction predictor can eliminate\\nmany of these stalls for negligible area cost.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The existing predictor covers backward branches (always taken), JAL (always\\ntaken), and returns (4-entry RAS). Forward conditional branches are always\\npr