ritical path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a small registered lookahead instruction replay predictor in `if_stage`.\\nOn each architecturally live fetch, fill a direct-mapped `{pc tag, instr}`\\ntable and, in parallel, look up the next fetch PC and register a one-cycle-\\nahead replay candidate. When `io_imemReady` later drops and the current PC\\nmatches a valid candidate, feed the cached instruction to decode and report\\nfetch-ready instead of injecting a bubble. Keep the normal ready-cycle path\\nlive-imem-first, invalidate replay candidates on redirect/flush, and avoid\\nfilling the table with killed wrong-path fetches. This should recover a\\nmeaningful fraction of random iStall loss while avoiding the immediate-decode\\nand predicted-target bookkeeping that made the earlier static branch/JAL\\npredictor regress on `bench`.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6...\n  Line 10: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260514-003-r3s2\", \"title\": \"Replay-Trained Next-PC Predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The current best `bench` result already proved that a tiny replay predictor can\\nclaw back a meaningful fraction of the tournament's random iStall loss without\\nputting decode or target-add logic on the IF critical path. What it still does\\nnot address is the compulsory redirect/flush cost on hot taken loop backedges\\nand direct calls, which CoreMark executes repeatedly.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current best `bench` result already proved that a tiny replay predictor can\\nclaw back a meaningful fraction of the tournament's random iStall loss without\\nputting decode or target-add logic on the IF critical path. What it still does\\nnot address is the compulsory redirect/flush cost on hot taken loop backedges\\nand direct calls, which CoreMark executes repeatedly.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Extend the existing replay-table frontend into a learned next-PC predictor that\\nis trained by EX with the actual resolved successor of taken BRANCH and direct\\nJAL instructions. Each table entry would keep the fetched instruction plus a\\nsmall predicted-successor field, letting IF steer to a previously seen target\\non a PC hit and carry that prediction through the pipe so EX only redirects on\\nmispredict. This keeps the successful replay-table structure, avoids immediate\\ndecode and target-add work in IF, and should recover stable loop/call bubbles\\nthat the current sequential-only replay predictor still pays every time.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add predicted-control metadata to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles so EX can validate a learned next-PC prediction against the resolved successor.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Upgrade the replay table into a tiny direct-mapped next-PC predictor that stores hot control-flow successors and can steer fetch to a ...\n\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gemini-3_5-flash-rep2/bench/gpt-5_4_xhigh/rep1/log.jsonl:\n  Line 4: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260514-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Static Backward-Branch IF Predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The current bench core resolves every conditional branch in EX and always\\nfetches `pc+4` until that point, so taken loop branches pay a two-bubble\\nwrong-path recovery cost. CoreMark spends much of its timed region in short\\nbackward loops, making a tiny static branch predictor a strong IPC lever\\nwithout the LUT and routing cost of a learned table, BTB, or return stack.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current bench core resolves every conditional branch in EX and always\\nfetches `pc+4` until that point, so taken loop branches pay a two-bubble\\nwrong-path recovery cost. CoreMark spends much of its timed region in short\\nbackward loops, making a tiny static branch predictor a strong IPC lever\\nwithout the LUT and routing cost of a learned table, BTB, or return stack.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a decode-light IF-stage predictor that recognizes legal B-type branches\\nand predicts backward branches taken when the branch immediate is negative.\\nIF computes the B immediate and predicted target, carries\\n`predicted_taken/predicted_target` through the existing pipeline metadata,\\nand EX redirects only when the resolved branch next PC disagrees with that\\nprediction. JAL and JALR stay on the current EX redirect path so the change\\nstays focused on the hottest control-flow class while keeping timing and LUT\\ngrowth small.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend `if_id_t` and `id_ex_t` with `predicted_taken` and `predicted_target` so IF can pass branch-prediction metadata into EX for validation.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add decode-light backward-branch prediction in fetch: recognize legal B-type encodings, form the branch immediate and target, and choose `pc+imm` instead of `pc+4` for predicted-taken backward branches when the target is wor...\n  Line 7: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260514-003-r2s2\", \"title\": \"Tiny PC-Indexed Taken BTB\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The last predictor attempt lost fitness because it lengthened the frontend\\ncritical path with `imem_data` decode and branch-immediate construction in IF.\\nBut the branch penalty is still real: this core waits until EX to correct any\\ntaken control flow, so hot loops and repeated calls keep paying wrong-path\\nfetch bubbles. The most promising predictor angle is therefore one that keeps\\nprediction state PC-indexed and decode-free on the fetch path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The last predictor attempt lost fitness because it lengthened the frontend\\ncritical path with `imem_data` decode and branch-immediate construction in IF.\\nBut the branch penalty is still real: this core waits until EX to correct any\\ntaken control flow, so hot loops and repeated calls keep paying wrong-path\\nfetch bubbles. The most promising predictor angle is therefore one that keeps\\nprediction state PC-indexed and decode-free on the fetch path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a very small direct-mapped branch target buffer that is consulted by PC\\nalone and predicts only previously-taken control-flow sites. IF should use a\\n`valid/tag/target` BTB hit to fetch the remembered target instead of `pc+4`,\\nwithout decoding the fetched instruction or rebuilding immediates on the hot\\npath. EX remains the point of truth for branch direction, JAL/JALR targets,\\ntraps, and RVFI; it simply compares the resolved next PC against the carried\\nprediction metadata, redirects on misses, and updates or invalidates the BTB\\nentry. This should recover much of the loop/call bubble cost while avoiding\\nthe timing regression seen from instruction-driven IF prediction logic.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the IF/ID and ID/EX payloads with compact prediction metadata so EX can validate a BTB hit against the...\n  Line 10: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260514-003-r3s2\", \"title\": \"One-Entry Loop Target Predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The bench core still pays a full control-flow bubble whenever a hot loop\\nbackedge is taken, but the two prior predictor attempts showed that this\\ndesign cannot afford much extra logic on the fetch critical path. The next\\npredictor should therefore recover only the highest-value target predictions\\nwhile keeping IF hardware smaller than both an instruction-driven predictor\\nand a multi-entry BTB.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The bench core still pays a full control-flow bubble whenever a hot loop\\nbackedge is taken, but the two prior predictor attempts showed that this\\ndesign cannot afford much extra logic on the fetch critical path. The next\\npredictor should therefore recover only the highest-value target predictions\\nwhile keeping IF hardware smaller than both an instruction-driven predictor\\nand a multi-entry BTB.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a single-entry loop-target predictor that remembers only the most recent\\ntaken backward branch and predicts again only on an exact PC match. IF would\\nconsult one registered `{valid, branch_pc, target_pc}` entry and choose the\\nremembered target instead of `pc+4` on a hit, with no `imem_data` decode,\\nimmediate construction, or table RAM lookup on the hot path. EX remains the\\npoint of truth: it validates the carried prediction, redirects only on\\nmispredicts, and updates or invalidates the single entry when a backward\\nbranch is taken or falls through. This keeps the predictor focused on\\nCoreMark's dominant tight loops while making the IF cost much smaller than\\nthe previously-regressing BTB approach.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the IF/ID and ID/EX payloads with compact prediction metadata so EX can validate a loop-target hit against the resolved next PC.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"...\n  Line 13: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260514-003-r4s2\", \"title\": \"Direction-Only Backward-Branch Hold Predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"Every prior bench predictor lost fitness because it inserted compare, target,\\nor decode logic directly into the IF `pc -> next_pc` path. But this core\\nstill wastes two sequential fetch slots on taken branches before EX resolves\\nthem. A predictor that reduces that waste without changing IF target\\nselection is the cleanest remaining control-flow lever.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Every prior bench predictor lost fitness because it inserted compare, target,\\nor decode logic directly into the IF `pc -> next_pc` path. But this core\\nstill wastes two sequential fetch slots on taken branches before EX resolves\\nthem. A predictor that reduces that waste without changing IF target\\nselection is the cleanest remaining control-flow lever.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Reuse the existing EX redirect point, but add a very cheap static direction\\npredictor that treats legal backward conditional branches as likely taken.\\nWhen such a branch reaches EX, `hazard_unit` should hold the frontend for one\\ncycle and inject a bubble into ID instead of allowing a second wrong-path\\nsequential fetch. If the branch is actually taken, EX redirects exactly as it\\ndoes today and the branch penalty drops from two wrong-path fetches to one.\\nIf the branch falls through, the only cost is a single bubble on the rare\\nloop exit. This stays off the timing-sensitive IF target path because it adds\\nno BTB lookup, no tag compare, and no target mux on `pc+4` selection.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a predictor-driven frontend-hold mode for backward conditional branches already in EX: stall PC, emit an IF NOP, and bubble ID for one cycle so taken branches fetch at most one wrong-path instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the existing `id_ex_w` branch/i...\n\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gemini-3_5-flash-rep2/bench/gemini-3_1-pro/rep3/log.jsonl:\n  Line 4: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260514-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"(slot 2 hypothesis-gen failed)\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"hypothesis_gen_failed: Hypothesis agent modified off-limits paths and was rolled back: ['cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv', 'cores/bench/rtl/core.sv', 'cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv']\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 1, \"hypothesi