 the baseline RV32IM CPU lacks any explicit branch prediction logic. Branch and jump resolutions currently trigger a redirect in the EX stage, which incurs a 2-cycle penalty due to flushes. My focus is now on how to mitigate this significant performance bottleneck.\\n\\n**Investigating instruction flow**\\n\\nI'm analyzing the cycle-by-cycle instruction flow during taken branches. It appears an instruction fetched immediately after the branch target is effectively flushed, even though a new instruction is fetched from the target in the subsequent cycle. I need to pinpoint where this lost instruction's decode is being suppressed.\\n\\n**Confirming penalty timing**\\n\\nI'm verifying the exact cycle penalty incurred by taken branches. My current understanding points to a 1-cycle bubble after the branch in the ID stage, not a 2-cycle flush, due to how the pipeline handles instruction fetches immediately following a branch instruction's execution.\\n\\n**Refining bubble calculation**\\n\\nMy recent a... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n3: {\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1779280115958,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1baa43bd5ffeTyBXYXMOzEdqBl\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e455bf8f3001q7NAdZovIAcRV1\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"93ec0378b3904f3cbe80b5eb3cbfcaf387373275\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e455bc4840013lDOxET7sAsN3q\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1baa43bd5ffeTyBXYXMOzEdqBl\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":43234,\"input\":40780,\"output\":23,\"reasoning\":2431,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":0}},\"cost\":0}}\n4: {\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1779280119242,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1baa43bd5ffeTyBXYXMOzEdqBl\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e455c05c8001wG9G9KRgzWHyI8\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e455bf91f001g21lYirxRsuBmi\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1baa43bd5ffeTyBXYXMOzEdqBl\",\"snapshot\":\"93ec0378b3904f3cbe80b5eb3cbfcaf387373275\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n5: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1779280119258,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1baa43bd5ffeTyBXYXMOzEdqBl\",\"part\":{\"type\"