03-r1s2\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Backward-Branch Taken Predictor\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"predictor\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current five-stage core resolves all branches and jumps in EX and fetches strictly pc+4 until that resolution, so every taken loop branch in CoreMark pays a two-instruction wrong-path flush. CoreMark's hot loops are dominated by short backward conditional branches whose direction is highly biased toward taken. A small static predictor can remove most loop-back redirect bubbles without adding a learned-state table, RAM, or speculative architectural state.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current five-stage core resolves all branches and jumps in EX and fetches strictly pc+4 until that resolution, so every taken loop branch in CoreMark pays a two-instruction wrong-path flush. CoreMark's hot loops are dominated by short backward conditional branches whose direction is highly biased toward taken. A small static predictor can remove most loop-back redirect bubbles without adding a learned-state table, RAM, or speculative architectural state.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Add a decode-light static branch predictor in IF that recognizes B-type instructions and predicts backward branches taken when the sign bit of the branch immediate is set. Compute the B immediate in IF, redirect the next PC to pc+imm for predicted-taken backward branches, and carry predicted_taken plus predicted_target through IF/ID and ID/EX. In EX, compare the actual branch result and target against the prediction, redirect onl... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n24: {\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1779280146286,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1baa43bd5ffeTyBXYXMOzEdqBl\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e455c6f6c001KQyD29XlqaJ366\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"9d0aad1c99865177b4e608700c71cda3a88516a3\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e455c5dc0001L95sXFnk2l80H1\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1baa43bd5ffeTyBXYXMOzEdqBl\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\