":\"reasoning.encrypted\",\"data\":\"\",\"id\":\"tool_read_megteEB7PlPNPYBlcTYR\",\"format\":\"google-gemini-v1\",\"index\":0}]}},\"id\":\"prt_e455d13a800194ul4oHqa1yQyP\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1baa43bd5ffeTyBXYXMOzEdqBl\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e455cfe9700168yaSNteHmOD1O\"}}\n48: {\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1779280188462,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1baa43bd5ffeTyBXYXMOzEdqBl\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e455d142d00169blFf8h5T7Nb6\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"93ec0378b3904f3cbe80b5eb3cbfcaf387373275\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e455cfe9700168yaSNteHmOD1O\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1baa43bd5ffeTyBXYXMOzEdqBl\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":182260,\"input\":182157,\"output\":57,\"reasoning\":46,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":0}},\"cost\":0}}\n49: {\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1779280193537,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1baa43bd5ffeTyBXYXMOzEdqBl\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e455d27ff001AwkOY2Nz0fH3WH\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e455d1455001cFA1GjiqC45HjT\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1baa43bd5ffeTyBXYXMOzEdqBl\",\"snapshot\":\"93ec0378b3904f3cbe80b5eb3cbfcaf387373275\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n50: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1779280193547,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1baa43bd5ffeTyBXYXMOzEdqBl\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"tool_read_Fb4wq1TBQlfMkUlCzEQ0\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gemini-3_5-flash-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260520-001-r1s0.yaml\"},\"output\":\"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gemini-3_5-flash-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260520-001-r1s0.yaml</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: id: hyp-20260520-001-r1s0\\n2: title: \\\"Precision load-use hazard detection and single 33-bit multiplier sharing\\\"\\n3: category: micro_opt\\n4: motivation: |\\n5:   The current 5-stage pipeline has two major microarchitectural bottlenecks:\\n6:   1. Spurious load-use stalls: The hazard unit stalls the pipeline whenever the rd of a load in EX matches the raw rs1/rs2 bits of the instruction in IF/ID. However, many instructions (like LUI, AUIPC, JAL, etc.) do not read rs1/rs2, and many immediate instructions do not read rs2. Treating those raw bits as active register source operands causes frequent, unnecessary 1-cycle pipeline stalls, especially for consecutive loads with immediate offsets.\\n7:   2. Multiplier combinational overhead: The ALU performs three independent 64-bit multiplications combinationally. This consumes a massive number of LUTs and limits Fmax due to the cascading delay in DSP blocks or carry chains.\\n8: hypothesis: |\\n9:   We propose two microarchitectural optimizations:\\n10:   1. Add precise instruction decode information for rs1/rs2 active read signals (if_id_rs1_read and if_id_rs2_read) into the hazard unit. Only trigger load-use stalls if the dependent instruction actually reads the register.\\n11:   2. Replace the three 64-bit multipliers in the ALU with a single shared 33-bit signed multiplier. By dynamically sign-extending or zero-extending the inputs based on the instruction type (sign... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n51: {\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1779280193722,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1baa43bd5ffeTyBXYXMOzEdqBl\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e455d28b9001cwE8sASV1QxvM5\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"93ec0378b3904f3cbe80b5eb3cbfcaf387373275\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e455d1455001cFA1GjiqC45HjT\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1baa43bd5ffeTyBXYXMOzEdqBl\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":182542,\"input\":182425,\"output\":78,\"reasoning\":39,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":0}},\"cost\":0}}\n52: {\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1779280198643,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1baa43bd5ffeTyBXYXMOzEdqBl\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e455d3bf20015HJe1e8ouvv666\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e455d28e3001WcC19fOW5oSj5B\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1baa43bd5ffeTyBXYXMOzEdqBl\",\"snapshot\":\"93ec0378b3904f3cbe80b5eb3cbfcaf387373275\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n\n(End of file - total 52 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1779280107769,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1baa43bd5ffeTyBXYXMOzEdqBl\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e455bd8f80019AO8R6SSCCs8Mc\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e455bc4840013lDOxET7sAsN3q\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1baa43bd5ffeTyBXYXMOzEdqBl\",\"snapshot\":\"93ec0378b3904f3cbe80b5eb3cbfcaf387373275\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1779280115661,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1baa43bd5ffeTyBXYXMOzEdqBl\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"glob\",\"callID\":\"tool_glob_t3tf0DEASk5N9fvz1m2j\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"pattern\":\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"},\"output\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gemini-3_5-flash-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\",\"metadata\":{\"count\":1,\"truncated\":false},\"title\":\"\",\"time\":{\"start\":1779280115649,\"end\":1779280115660}},\"metadata\":{\"openrouter\":{\"reasoning_details\":[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"**Developing predictor hypothesis**\\n\\nI am currently exploring architectural hypotheses focused on prediction to enhance the `cores/bench` RV32IM CPU. My primary goal is to boost the CoreMark iter/sec fitness metric, which directly relates to CoreMark iterations per cycle and Fmax on the Tang Nano 20K FPGA. This is my contribution to the diversity slot for this round.\\n\\n**Analyzing current redirect mechanism**\\n\\nI've confirmed the baseline RV32IM CPU lacks any explicit branch prediction logic. Branch and jump resolutions currently trigger a redirect in the EX stage, which incurs a 2-cycle penalty due to flushes. My focus is now on how to mitigate this significant performance bottleneck.\\n\\n**Investigating instruction flow**\\n\\nI'm analyzing the cycle-by-cycle instruction flow during taken branches. It appears an instruction fetched immediately after the branch target is effectively flushed, even though a new instruction is fetched from the target in the subsequent cycle. I need to pinpoint where this lost instruction's decode is being suppressed.\\n\\n**Confirming penalty timing**\\n\\nI'm verifying the exact cycle penalty incurred by taken branches. My current understanding points to a 1-cycle bubble after the branch in the ID stage, not a 2-cycle flush, due to how the pipeline handles instruction fetches immediately following a branch instruction's execution.\\n\\n**Refining bubble calculation**\\n\\nMy recent a... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1779280115958,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1baa43bd5ffeTyBXYXMOzEdqBl\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e455bf8f3001q7NAdZovIAcRV1\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"93ec0378b3904f3cbe80b5eb3cbfcaf387373275\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e455bc4840013lDOxET7sAsN3q\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1baa43bd5ffeTyBXYXMOzEdqBl\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":43234,\"input\":40780,\"output\":23,\"reasoning\":2431,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":0}},\"cost\":0}}\n{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1779280119242,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1baa43bd5ffeTyBXYXMOzEdqBl\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e455c05c8001wG9G9KRgzWHyI8\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e455bf91f001g21lYirxRsuBmi\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1baa43bd5ffeTyBXYXMOzEdqBl\",\"snapshot\":\"93ec0378b3904f3cbe80b5eb3cbfcaf387373275\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1779280119258,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1baa43bd5ffeTyBXYXMOzEdqBl\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"tool_read_Nz2Yw953Rg4GrQqGLI74\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gemini-3_5-flash-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"},\"output\":\"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gemini-3_5-flash-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: {\\\"id\\\": \\\"baseline-bench-0ff0685\\\", \\\"t