` to `correct_next_pc`.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 15, \"confidence\": \"high\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add `logic [31:0] pc_next_fetched;` to both `if_id_t` and `id_ex_t` structs (immediately after `pc`).\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add BTB state: `localparam BTB_ENTRIES = 64; logic [31:0] btb_target[0:63]; logic [31:0] btb_tag[0:63]; logic btb_valid[0:63];`.\\nAdd BTB update ports: `input btb_update, input [31:0] btb_update_pc, input [31:0] btb_update_target, input btb_update_valid`.\\nAdd a synchronous...","metadata":{"matches":1,"truncated":false},"title":"hyp-20260514-003-r5s2","time":{"start":1779280288112,"end":1779280288121}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"**Exploring Predictor Options**\n\nI'm currently examining `cores/bench/rtl/`, noting its lack of prediction logic. My focus is on identifying the cleanest, most robust predictor to introduce. I'm specifically analyzing `hyp-20260514-003-r6s2` from `bench/kimi` as a starting point for this investigation.\n\n**Evaluating Predictor Options**\n\nI'm now understanding why static prediction from `imem_data` is so detrimental to Fmax. The path involves off-chip reads and extensive combinational logic, significantly impacting timing. A BTB, conversely, offers a much cleaner and faster solution by using PC indexing for quick target retrieval.\n\n","format":"google-gemini-v1","index":0},{"type":"reasoning.encrypted","data":"","id":"tool_grep_UQ28nLNAoKlnCiBi5Esw","format":"google-gemini-v1","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_e455e996d001JloWk1DQueCj84","sessionID":"ses_1baa43bd5ffeTyBXYXMOzEdqBl","messageID":"msg_e455e7f14001IT5IJnJy0yVYxO"}}
