{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1779280412829,"sessionID":"ses_1baa43bd5ffeTyBXYXMOzEdqBl","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"tool_write_cPF1YsjKzBHjlRJsUEIo","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gemini-3_5-flash-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260520-003-r1s2.yaml","content":"id: hyp-20260520-003-r1s2\ntitle: \"Two-bank registered lookahead instruction replay predictor with static branch/JAL predecode\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The baseline RV32IM core always fetches sequentially and resolves all control flow in EX, incurring a 2-cycle flush penalty on every taken branch and jump. Additionally, the apples-to-apples evaluation environment drives ~22% random instruction-memory stalls, injecting significant bubble counts into the pipeline. Conventional branch predictors or target buffers often regress FPGA Fmax by putting instruction decode, target adders, tag comparisons, or return-address stacks directly on the timing-sensitive fetch next-PC path.\nhypothesis: |\n  We propose a timing-clean, high-performance two-bank registered lookahead instruction replay predictor combined with stateless static branch/JAL predecode in the IF stage:\n  1. Replay Table: A 256-entry (128 per bank), two-bank direct-mapped replay table indexed by pc[8:2] and tagged by pc[31:9]. It caches successfully fetched instruction words and looks up the next-PC replay candidate one cycle ahead, completely removing table reads and tag comparisons from the same-cycle IF decision path.\n  2. iStall Hiding: When imem_ready drops, IF supplies the registered lookahead instruction and asserts fetch-ready, converting random iStall bubbles into zero-wait fetch cycles.\n  3. Static Predecode: Within IF, combinationally predecode JAL and backward conditional branches (negative displacement) from the fetched/replayed instruction, update the fetch next_pc early, and propagate the prediction.\n  4. EX Validation: EX verifies the prediction and asserts redirect only on a mismatch (mispredict), turning correct predictions into 0-cycle control transfers.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 12\n  confidence: high\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Extend if_id_t and id_ex_t with predicted_taken and predicted_target fields.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Implement the static branch/JAL predecode, the 2-bank 128-set registered lookahead instruction replay predictor (tag/valid/instr/mru arrays), and lookahead candidate tracking.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch the predicted next-PC metadata fields into the ID/EX register.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Replace unconditional branch/jump redirects with mispredict-only redirection.\"\n"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gemini-3_5-flash-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260520-003-r1s2.yaml","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260520-003-r1s2.yaml","time":{"start":1779280412826,"end":1779280412829}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"**Completing Instruction Stage**\n\nI've finalized the registered lookahead instruction replay table for the instruction fetch stage, integrating static branch prediction. I'm now assessing its impact on CPI and Fmax for potential inclusion in the benchmark suite.\n\n**Refining Instruction Fetch**\n\nI'm assessing the fitness impact of integrating static branch prediction with a registered lookahead instruction replay cache. This combination is showing significant IPC gains by eliminating taken branch bubbles and converting random stalls into instruction fetches, while preserving Fmax.\n\n**Developing Instruction Replay**\n\nI'm exploring a two-bank registered lookahead instruction replay predictor combined with static branch and JAL predecode. This approach aims to address sequential fetch limitations and instruction memory stalls, potentially enhancing IPC without impacting Fmax.\n\n**Optimizing Instruction Flow**\n\nI'm implementing a two-banked replay table, direct-mapped via PC, with a focus on caching fetched instruction words. This setup allows for a one-cycle ahead replay candidate lookup, effectively removing table reads and tag comparisons from the critical IF decision path and hiding iStall bubbles.\n\n**Implementing Instruction Logic**\n\nI'm now focusing on the RTL implementation. This involves adding the static branch/JAL predecode and the two-banked registered lookahead predictor to `if_stage.sv`. Additionally, I'm ensuring predicted next-PC metadata is latched correctly into the ID/EX register and modifying the EX stage to handle mispredict-only redirection for branches and jumps.\n\n**Validating Instruction Path**\n\nI'm confirming the absolute path for the YAML configuration file and verifying the existence of its parent directory. I'm now meticulously constructing the YAML content, focusing on accurately detailing the hypothesis for the two-bank registered lookahead predictor with static branch and JAL predecode.\n\n**Finalizing Replay Table Logic**\n\nI'm now thoroughly reviewing the logic for the 256-entry, two-bank registered lookahead replay table. My focus is on ensuring its direct-mapped indexing and tag comparison are robust, aiming to eliminate table operations from the critical fetch path for enhanced performance.\n\n**Implementing Replay Logic**\n\nI'm currently implementing the static branch/JAL predecode and a two-bank registered lookahead instruction replay predictor within `if_stage.sv`. This involves tracking lookahead candidates, extending `if_id_t` and `id_ex_t` with predicted taken/target fields, and modifying the EX stage for mispredict-only redirection.\n\n**Clarifying File Paths**\n\nI'm confirming the exact format required for file paths in the hypothesis YAML. It appears `rtl/<filename>` is the precise short form expected, relative to the RTL directory, and the orchestrator handles the full resolution.\n\n","format":"google-gemini-v1","index":0},{"type":"reasoning.encrypted","data":"","id":"tool_write_cPF1YsjKzBHjlRJsUEIo","format":"google-gemini-v1","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_e45608097001x13uFj5G6V9Vm7","sessionID":"ses_1baa43bd5ffeTyBXYXMOzEdqBl","messageID":"msg_e45604a99001l3M9tSIprD7UlP"}}
