{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1779282757658,"sessionID":"ses_1ba7d2a8fffeaRs7VH30axjNA1","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"tool_write_c3ap6S2Yjd8mgdGUQXHt","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gemini-3_5-flash-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260520-003-r2s2.yaml","content":"id: hyp-20260520-003-r2s2\ntitle: \"Lookahead 128-entry 2-bit Bimodal Branch History Table (BHT) Predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The current RV32IM core resolves conditional branch instructions in the EX stage, resulting in a 2-cycle penalty for every mispredicted or taken forward branch. While static prediction (taken for backward, not-taken for forward) helps for simple loops, it fails on highly-branchy control flows like CoreMark's inner benchmarks (e.g. state machines, matrix lookups, data-dependent loops). Introducing a dynamic Branch History Table (BHT) allows the core to adaptively learn branch behavior, reducing pipeline flushes and significantly increasing IPC without degrading Fmax.\nhypothesis: |\n  We propose adding a timing-clean, fully-registered 128-entry 2-bit Bimodal Branch History Table (BHT) in the IF stage, coupled with EX-stage resolution and BHT update feedback.\n  1. 128-entry BHT: An array of 128 2-bit saturating counters indexed by pc[8:2] (the same index as the instruction replay table).\n  2. 1-Cycle Lookahead Lookup: To preserve FPGA Fmax, we query the BHT one cycle ahead using next_pc[8:2] and register the 2-bit prediction counter. This keeps BHT reads completely off the same-cycle next-PC critical path.\n  3. Dynamic Prediction: In the IF stage, if a conditional branch is fetched/replayed, we predict it as taken if the registered BHT counter's MSB is 1, and not-taken otherwise, overriding the static predictor.\n  4. EX-Stage Feedback: The registered BHT counter value is passed down the pipeline via if_id and id_ex registers. Upon branch resolution in the EX stage, the BHT is updated dynamically via dedicated update ports back to the IF stage.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 12\n  confidence: high\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add a 2-bit bht_val field to both if_id_t and id_ex_t pipeline-bundle structures.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Implement the 128-entry 2-bit BHT, the next-PC lookahead BHT read register, the dynamic branch prediction override using BHT states, and the BHT write update logic.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch the 2-bit bht_val field from the if_id combinational bundle into the id_ex register.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Calculate and output BHT update control signals (enable, index, old value, actual outcome) based on the resolved branch in EX.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the BHT update control signals from the EX stage back to the IF stage.\"\n"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gemini-3_5-flash-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260520-003-r2s2.yaml","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260520-003-r2s2.yaml","time":{"start":1779282757654,"end":1779282757657}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"**Discovering Log Files**\n\nI've realized the files I was looking for are dotfiles, explaining why glob didn't find them. My next step is to use the `write` tool to create our hypothesis file, after composing and verifying the YAML block internally.\n\n**Formulating Hypothesis Details**\n\nI'm now focusing on refining the YAML block for our hypothesis, specifically confirming the hypothesis ID and ensuring the `motivation` and `hypothesis` fields accurately capture the proposed BHT implementation and its benefits. I'll then proceed to write this to the hypothesis file using the `write` tool.\n\n**Implementing Branch Prediction**\n\nI'm actively working on integrating the 1-cycle lookahead branch history table (BHT) lookup within the IF stage. This involves registering the 2-bit prediction counter to maintain FPGA Fmax. I'm also implementing dynamic prediction logic that overrides static predictors based on the BHT counter's MSB, and ensuring feedback from the EX stage for BHT updates.\n\n**Refining Predictor Logic**\n\nI'm now concentrating on the precise implementation details of dynamic branch prediction override and BHT write update logic within the `id_stage.sv` and `ex_stage.sv` files. I'm also ensuring correct wiring back to the IF stage via `core.sv`. The hypothesis schema appears to be valid.\n\n","format":"google-gemini-v1","index":0},{"type":"reasoning.encrypted","data":"","id":"tool_write_c3ap6S2Yjd8mgdGUQXHt","format":"google-gemini-v1","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_e45844813001KagmsO8eJ3AZsF","sessionID":"ses_1ba7d2a8fffeaRs7VH30axjNA1","messageID":"msg_e45842577001nH49OJqAFFXQpf"}}
