{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1779283067851,"sessionID":"ses_1ba7a1dc7ffeENx8ai3mJ0P6CY","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"tool_read_SWVVmV416HYVEuAjzQoH","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gemini-3_5-flash-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260520-002-r2s1/formal/run_all.sh"},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gemini-3_5-flash-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260520-002-r2s1/formal/run_all.sh</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: #!/usr/bin/env bash\n2: # Run riscv-formal checks against the current $RTL_DIR/*.sv.\n3: # Requires: formal/riscv-formal cloned (manual clone or `git submodule init`).\n4: #\n5: # Stages every $RTL_DIR/*.sv plus wrapper.sv + the chosen checks config under\n6: # the riscv-formal tree, then runs sby -> bitwuzla via the framework's\n7: # generated makefile. Tallies PASS/FAIL by inspecting each task's\n8: # logfile.txt.\n9: #\n10: # Usage: bash formal/run_all.sh [checks-cfg-path]\n11: #   default: formal/checks.cfg       (fast, ALTOPS, used by orchestrator)\n12: #   deep   : formal/checks-deep.cfg  (no ALTOPS, proves M-ext arithmetic)\n13: #\n14: # Env vars (orchestrator-driven, override $1 and defaults):\n15: #   WRAPPER     — path to wrapper SV (default formal/wrapper.sv)\n16: #   CHECKS_CFG  — path to checks config (default formal/checks.cfg)\n17: # When BOTH are unset, the script auto-detects nret from\n18: # cores/$CORE_NAME/core.yaml: nret=1 routes to wrapper_si.sv +\n19: # checks_si.cfg; nret=2 (or absent) uses the defaults. Agents\n20: # invoking `bash formal/run_all.sh` directly therefore get the\n21: # right wrapper without needing to know the env-var plumbing.\n22: set -e\n23: \n24: if [ -z \"${RTL_DIR:-}\" ] || [ -z \"${CORE_NAME:-}\" ]; then\n25:   echo \"ERROR: formal/run_all.sh requires RTL_DIR and CORE_NAME env vars.\" >&2\n26:   echo \"  Example: RTL_DIR=cores/v1/rtl CORE_NAME=v1 bash formal/run_all.sh formal/checks.cfg\" >&2\n27:   exit 2\n28: fi\n29: \n30: SCRIPT_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\"\n31: PROJECT_ROOT=\"$(cd \"$SCRIPT_DIR/..\" && pwd)\"\n32: RISCV_FORMAL=\"$SCRIPT_DIR/riscv-formal\"\n33: # PID-suffixed work dir + log so two concurrent invocations (e.g., the\n34: # agent self-checking mid-implementation while the orchestrator runs\n35: # its end-of-iteration eval) don't race on `rm -rf checks/` or\n36: # truncate each other's last_run.log. Was observed live in the\n37: # nret=1 verify run: two slots got broken: make_failed_during_execution\n38: # because the agent invoked `bash formal/run_all.sh` 6+ times in quick\n39: # succession, each invocation wiping the previous one's checks/ dir\n40: # mid-SBY (yosys-smtbmc crashed with `FileNotFoundError: 'engine_0/trace0.vcd'`).\n41: # genchecks.py derives @core@ from cwd's basename (genchecks.py:39), so\n42: # the PID-suffixed dir maps cleanly to @core@=\"$CORE_NAME-$$\".\n43: CORE_DIR=\"$RISCV_FORMAL/cores/$CORE_NAME-$$\"\n44: LOG=\"$SCRIPT_DIR/last_run-$$.log\"\n45: \n46: # Auto-detect single-issue cores from core.yaml when WRAPPER + CHECKS_CFG\n47: # are both unset and $1 (checks-cfg-path) wasn't given either. Explicit\n48: # env vars or $1 still win. Uses python3 to parse YAML robustly — bash\n49: # grep would mis-handle quoted/indented variants and break on the next\n50: # yaml schema bump.\n51: CORE_YAML=\"$PROJECT_ROOT/cores/$CORE_NAME/core.yaml\"\n52: if [ -z \"${WRAPPER:-}\" ] && [ -z \"${CHECKS_CFG:-}\" ] && [ -z \"${1:-}\" ] \\\n53:    && [ -f \"$CORE_YAML\" ]; then\n54:     # Pass the path via env var so the python literal stays free of any\n55:     # bash-substituted strings that could break on quoting / spaces.\n56:     NRET=$(CORE_YAML=\"$CORE_YAML\" python3 -c '\n57: import os, yaml\n58: try:\n59:     d = yaml.safe_load(open(os.environ[\"CORE_YAML\"]).read()) or {}\n60:     print(int(d.get(\"nret\", 2)))\n61: except Exception:\n62:     print(2)\n63: ' 2>/dev/null)\n64:     if [ \"$NRET\" = \"1\" ]; then\n65:         WRAPPER=\"$SCRIPT_DIR/wrapper_si.sv\"\n66:         CHECKS_CFG=\"$SCRIPT_DIR/checks_si.cfg\"\n67:         echo \"[run_all.sh] auto-detected nret=1 from $CORE_YAML; using wrapper_si.sv + checks_si.cfg\"\n68:     fi\n69: fi\n70: \n71: CHECKS_CFG=\"${CHECKS_CFG:-${1:-$SCRIPT_DIR/checks.cfg}}\"\n72: WRAPPER=\"${WRAPPER:-$SCRIPT_DIR/wrapper.sv}\"\n73: if [ ! -f \"$CHECKS_CFG\" ]; then\n74:     echo \"ERROR: checks.cfg not found at $CHECKS_CFG\"\n75:     exit 1\n76: fi\n77: if [ ! -f \"$WRAPPER\" ]; then\n78:     echo \"ERROR: wrapper not found at $WRAPPER\"\n79:     exit 1\n80: fi\n81: \n82: if [ ! -d \"$RISCV_FORMAL\" ]; then\n83:     echo \"ERROR: formal/riscv-formal not found. Clone it:\"\n84:     echo \"  git clone https://github.com/YosysHQ/riscv-formal $SCRIPT_DIR/riscv-formal\"\n85:     exit 1\n86: fi\n87: \n88: # OSS CAD Suite for consistent yosys / sby / bitwuzla. Homebrew yosys\n89: # combined with Homebrew bitwuzla has been observed to BrokenPipe inside\n90: # yosys-smtbmc.\n91: if [ -d \"$PROJECT_ROOT/.toolchain/oss-cad-suite/bin\" ]; then\n92:     export PATH=\"$PROJECT_ROOT/.toolchain/oss-cad-suite/bin:$PATH\"\n93: fi\n94: \n95: # Reap stale per-PID work dirs + logs whose owning process has exited.\n96: # Bounds disk growth from long runs (an agent that invokes run_all.sh\n97: # dozens of times leaves dozens of $CORE_NAME-<pid>/ dirs otherwise).\n98: # kill -0 returns 0 iff <pid> exists; non-existent / non-numeric names\n99: # fall through to cleanup. Concurrent live runs are protected because\n100: # their PIDs are still alive.\n101: shopt -s nullglob\n102: for stale in \"$RISCV_FORMAL/cores/$CORE_NAME-\"*; do\n103:     pid=\"${stale##*-}\"\n104:     if [[ \"$pid\" =~ ^[0-9]+$ ]] && ! kill -0 \"$pid\" 2>/dev/null; then\n105:         rm -rf \"$stale\"\n106:     fi\n107: done\n108: for stale_log in \"$SCRIPT_DIR\"/last_run-*.log; do\n109:     pid=\"${stale_log##*-}\"\n110:     pid=\"${pid%.log}\"\n111:     if [[ \"$pid\" =~ ^[0-9]+$ ]] && ! kill -0 \"$pid\" 2>/dev/null; then\n112:         rm -f \"$stale_log\"\n113:     fi\n114: done\n115: shopt -u nullglob\n116: \n117: # Truncate the run log; genchecks + make are tee'd here in full.\n118: : > \"$LOG\"\n119: \n120: # Stage rtl + wrapper + the chosen checks config under the framework's\n121: # expected layout. genchecks.py looks for \"checks.cfg\" by name, so the\n122: # selected config is always copied to that filename in the core dir.\n123: mkdir -p \"$CORE_DIR\"\n124: # Clear stale .sv files first. Without this, a hypothesis that renames or\n125: # deletes a module in rtl/ leaves a ghost copy in $CORE_DIR from the\n126: # previous run, and genchecks/yosys silently picks up the old file\n127: # instead of the new one. CLAUDE.md explicitly grants hypotheses the\n128: # right to rename/delete files in rtl/, so this cleanup is required.\n129: rm -f \"$CORE_DIR\"/*.sv\n130: cp \"$PROJECT_ROOT/$RTL_DIR\"/*.sv \"$CORE_DIR/\"\n131: cp \"$WRAPPER\"                   \"$CORE_DIR/wrapper.sv\"\n132: \n133: # Stage checks.cfg with [verilog-files] auto-derived from actual rtl/\n134: # contents instead of the cfg's hardcoded list. The shipped checks.cfg\n135: # enumerates the V0 baseline filenames; CLAUDE.md grants hypotheses the\n136: # right to add new modules, split a stage into multiple files, or rename\n137: # files in rtl/. Hardcoding silently fails on those restructurings (or\n138: # elaborates a stale ghost). Strip the original [verilog-files] section\n139: # and rebuild from the glob, with core_pkg.sv first and wrapper.sv last.\n140: STAGED_CFG=\"$CORE_DIR/checks.cfg\"\n141: awk '/^\\[verilog-files\\]/{exit} {print}' \"$CHECKS_CFG\" > \"$STAGED_CFG\"\n142: {\n143:     echo \"[verilog-files]\"\n144:     [ -f \"$CORE_DIR/core_pkg.sv\" ] && \\\n145:         echo \"@basedir@/cores/@core@/core_pkg.sv\"\n146:     for f in \"$CORE_DIR\"/*.sv; do\n147:         name=\"$(basename \"$f\")\"\n148:         [ \"$name\" = \"core_pkg.sv\" ] && continue\n149:         [ \"$name\" = \"wrapper.sv\" ] && continue\n150:         echo \"@basedir@/cores/@core@/$name\"\n151:     done\n152:     echo \"@basedir@/cores/@core@/wrapper.sv\"\n153: } >> \"$STAGED_CFG\"\n154: \n155: # genchecks.py derives @core@ from the cwd's basename (genchecks.py:39),\n156: # so cd-ing into $CORE_DIR (= $RISCV_FORMAL/cores/$CORE_NAME-$$) yields\n157: # @core@=\"$CORE_NAME-$$\". The [verilog-files] lines we just wrote\n158: # reference that @core@, so all paths resolve into this PID-private dir.\n159: cd \"$CORE_DIR\"\n160: rm -rf checks/\n161: echo \"=== genchecks ===\" | tee -a \"$LOG\"\n162: python3 ../../checks/genchecks.py >> \"$LOG\" 2>&1\n163: cd checks\n164: \n165: JOBS=\"${JOBS:-$(sysctl -n hw.ncpu 2>/dev/null || nproc 2>/dev/null || echo 4)}\"\n166: echo \"=== make -j$JOBS -k ===\" | tee -a \"$LOG\"\n167: # Tee full output to LOG; show filtered progress on stdout. `-k` keeps\n168: # going past per-check errors so the .sby tally below sees every result\n169: # (NRET=2 means a few `_ch1` checks may PREUNSAT-error on single-issue\n170: # cores; without -k make stops on first error and 95+ checks never run,\n171: # producing a misleading failure list of unbuilt directories).\n172: make -j\"$JOBS\" -k -f makefile 2>&1 \\\n173:     | tee -a \"$LOG\" \\\n174:     | grep -E \"^(make|SBY|yosys|==|ERROR)\" || true\n175: \n176: shopt -s nullglob\n177: PASS=0; FAIL=0; FAILED=()\n178: for sby_file in *.sby; do\n179:     name=\"${sby_file%.sby}\"\n180:     log=\"$name/logfile.txt\"\n181:     if grep -q \"DONE (PASS\" \"$log\" 2>/dev/null; then\n182:         PASS=$((PASS+1))\n183:     elif [[ \"$name\" == *_ch1 ]] && grep -q \"Status: PREUNSAT\" \"$log\" 2>/dev/null; then\n184:         # Vacuous pass on channel-1 checks. NRET=2 contract: when a\n185:         # single-issue hypothesis ties io_rvfi_valid_1 to 0, the per-channel\n186:         # BMC's assumption (rvfi_valid_1=1) is unsatisfiable, and SBY\n187:         # reports Status: PREUNSAT (rc=16). The property holds vacuously\n188:         # over the empty set of ch1-valid traces — a legitimate pass.\n189:         # Dual-issue hypotheses make the assumption satisfiable, so this\n190:         # branch never matches and the regular DONE (PASS branch covers it.\n191:         PASS=$((PASS+1))\n192:     else\n193:         FAIL=$((FAIL+1)); FAILED+=(\"$name\")\n194:     fi\n195: done\n196: TOTAL=$((PASS+FAIL))\n197: if [ $TOTAL -eq 0 ]; then\n198:     FAIL=1\n199:     FAILED+=(\"no_checks_generated\")\n200: fi\n201: \n202: echo \"\"\n203: echo \"Formal: $PASS passed, $FAIL failed\"\n204: if [ $FAIL -gt 0 ]; then\n205:     echo \"Failed: ${FAILED[*]}\"\n206:     # Surface the FIRST failing check's logfile tail. tools/eval/formal.py\n207:     # captures this script's stdout/stderr into formal['detail'] and the\n208:     # orchestrator now records that in experiments/log.jsonl, so what we\n209:     # print here is what shows up as the diagnostic for the failed run.\n210:     first=\"${FAILED[0]}\"\n211:     if [ -f \"$first/logfile.txt\" ]; then\n212:         echo \"\"\n213:         echo \"--- $first/logfile.txt (last 30 lines) ---\"\n214:         tail -30 \"$first/logfile.txt\"\n215:     fi\n216:     echo \"\"\n217:     echo \"Full run log: $LOG\"\n218:     echo \"Per-check logs in: $CORE_DIR/checks/<check>/logfile.txt\"\n219: fi\n220: [ $FAIL -eq 0 ]\n\n(End of file - total 220 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Run riscv-formal checks against the current $RTL_DIR/*.sv.\n# Requires: formal/riscv-formal cloned (manual clone or `git submodule init`).\n#\n# Stages every $RTL_DIR/*.sv plus wrapper.sv + the chosen checks config under\n# the riscv-formal tree, then runs sby -> bitwuzla via the framework's\n# generated makefile. Tallies PASS/FAIL by inspecting each task's\n# logfile.txt.\n#\n# Usage: bash formal/run_all.sh [checks-cfg-path]\n#   default: formal/checks.cfg       (fast, ALTOPS, used by orchestrator)\n#   deep   : formal/checks-deep.cfg  (no ALTOPS, proves M-ext arithmetic)\n#\n# Env vars (orchestrator-driven, override $1 and defaults):\n#   WRAPPER     — path to wrapper SV (default formal/wrapper.sv)\n#   CHECKS_CFG  — path to checks config (default formal/checks.cfg)\n# When BOTH are unset, the script auto-detects nret from\n# cores/$CORE_NAME/core.yaml: nret=1 routes to wrapper_si.sv +\n# checks_si.cfg; nret=2 (or absent) uses the defaults. Agents\n# invoking `bash formal/run_all.sh` directly therefore get the","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"formal/run_all.sh","time":{"start":1779283067836,"end":1779283067850}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"**Examining the Error**\n\nI'm meticulously dissecting this error output. My current focus is on pinpointing the exact cause within the provided file path. I'm scrutinizing each segment of the path to identify any discrepancies or misconfigurations that might be triggering this issue.\n\n","format":"google-gemini-v1","index":0},{"type":"reasoning.encrypted","data":"","id":"tool_read_SWVVmV416HYVEuAjzQoH","format":"google-gemini-v1","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_e458903b8001HmLB2M319N7Cqo","sessionID":"ses_1ba7a1dc7ffeENx8ai3mJ0P6CY","messageID":"msg_e4588e524001eF4pt4p9ZuyYL9"}}
